<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    Agent's cross-section surface. The leaf existed as its own project because one consumer
    sat in Base: AgentConversationRetentionJob in Humans.Infrastructure/Jobs, reaching the
    section through IAgentConversationRetention. **That is no longer true** — the job moved
    into Humans.Agent/Contracts/ at G5 lane 5b-5 (nobodies-collective/Humans#866), and
    AnthropicBalanceProvider never counted (it implements a Base-owned connector interface
    that the section consumes, not the other way round).

    Re-derived at that lane, every remaining consumer is in Shell: HelpWidgetViewComponent
    and the two health checks read IAgentAvailability, AgentPreloadAugmentor implements
    IAgentPreloadAugmentor and resolves AgentSectionKeys. Shell references Humans.Agent
    directly, so a Contracts/ *folder* would now serve all of them and this project could
    fold into one. Humans.UI names no type from here — its one mention is a <see cref> in a
    doc comment. Left standing deliberately: collapsing a leaf is Peter's call, not a job
    move's side effect.

    References Humans.Interfaces only.
  -->

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Humans.Interfaces\Humans.Interfaces.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
